  "source_type": "literature",
  "citation": "López-López et al. Interrogation of Essentiality in the Reconstructed Haemophilus influenzae Metabolic Network Identifies Lipid Metabolism Antimicrobial Targets: Preclinical Evaluation of a FabH β-Ketoacyl-ACP Synthase Inhibitor. mSystems (2022). DOI: 10.1128/msystems.01459-21. [PMC9040583]",
  "doi": "10.1128/msystems.01459-21",
  "url": "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC9040583/",
  "notes": "Extracted from the primary paper (snippet: mCDM formulation only allowed uptake of inorganic salts and essential vitamins for growth (i.e., choline, pantothenate, and folate).). Component names mapped to BiGG (see mapping_confidence); presence-based bounds unless the paper gave exchange bounds; concentration_mM where units allowed. Extraction confidence: medium.",
  "verification": "paper-verified (corrected via workflow)",
  "verification_evidence": "The uptake of pyruvate, glucose, NAD, inosine, and uracil was allowed as main nutrients in all cases ... whereas mCDM formulation only allowed uptake of inorganic salts and essential vitamins for growth (i.e., choline, pantothenate, and folate).",
  "verification_confidence": "medium",
